    {
      "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
      "name": {% if sx_L == 'en' %}"Elenchon Atlas — Welder Qualification Tracking"{% else %}{{ sx_name | jsonify }}{% endif %},
      "applicationCategory": "BusinessApplication",
      "applicationSubCategory": "Welder Qualification Management Software",
      "operatingSystem": "Cloud / Web",
      "description": {% if sx_L == 'en' %}"Cloud welder qualification (WPQ) management software that keeps track of which welders hold which qualifications and when each one runs out. Each welder qualification is a record with its own expiry date and continuity date, tracked as two independent clocks and warned separately. A welder-by-process grid shows each cell's soonest-due qualification, colour-coded and fully filterable by welder, process, standard or recorded qualification detail; requalification is recorded behind a password signature as an immutable, attributed stamp; the qualification certificate can optionally be attached and viewed on the record; and every qualification a welder has ever held is retained. Due dates surface on the dashboard and, when switched on, by email to a recipient list. Qualification variables are pre-built for ISO 9606, ASME IX and AWS, and custom fields can be added. It records and warns — it does not judge whether a qualification is valid. Part of Elenchon Atlas, alongside cloud WPS management. From Delteris."{% else %}{{ sx_desc | jsonify }}{% endif %},
{% if sx_L == 'en' %}      "keywords": "welder qualification management software, WPQ software, welder qualification tracking, welder qualification tracker, welder continuity tracking, welder certification tracking, ISO 9606 welder qualification, ASME IX welder qualification, welding qualification expiry reminder, welder ticket tracking",{% endif %}
{% if sx_L == 'en' %}      "featureList": [
        "One record per welder per qualification, capturing the full set of qualification variables the standard defines (process, position, material group, thickness and diameter ranges, backing, and more)",
        "Two independent clocks — an expiry date plus a reverification interval (ISO reverify-every-X-months or ASME qualified-for-X-months) — tracked and warned separately",
        "Editable warning lead times (for example a month out, two weeks, the week of)",
        "Welder-by-process qualification grid, each cell showing that process's soonest-due qualification, colour-coded",
        "Fully filterable roster — by welder ID, process, standard, or recorded qualification detail such as whether knowledge was tested",
        "Per-welder detail view with active records and full retained history",
        "Email reminders to a recipient list (up to ten addresses), opt-in, plus dashboard visibility",
        "Requalification recorded behind a password signature as an immutable, attributed stamp",
        "Optional qualification certificate attached to the record and viewable (scan, PDF or image)",
        "Side-by-side file viewer — choose any document on each side (WPS to WPS, WPQ to WPQR, certificate to WPS)",
        "Retained history — every qualification a welder has ever held is kept, never overwritten",
        "Pre-built qualification variables for ISO 9606, ASME IX and AWS, plus custom fields",
        "Records and warns; does not rule on whether a qualification is valid"
